  "equipment_type": "Self-contained vertical unit ventilator controller (classroom)",
  "applies_to": "Modine ClassMate (CMD/CMP/CMS) and SchoolMate (SMG/SMW) vertical classroom units running Modine Controls System program series 1.",
  "summary": "ClassMate and SchoolMate classroom units use a Carel pCOOEM+ controller; an optional BMS card gives BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP/Ethernet (LonWorks and Modbus are other options). The BMS can switch the unit on and off, send an occupied command, reset alarms, send a heartbeat and write cooling, heating offset, unoccupied, standby, humidity and CO2 setpoints. It reads temperatures, humidity, CO2, damper and valve positions, relay outputs, digital inputs and individual alarms.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Modine Controls System program version series 1",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object names here are the Carel variable names printed in the manual; the BACnet column gives only the object address (AVn / BVn). Check the names your BACnet card reports.",
    "Carel analog variables are AV 1-24, Carel integer variables are AV 1001-1017 and digital variables are BV 1-39.",
    "The manual marks several fan, wheel and fan-alarm rows with an asterisk but prints no footnote for it.",
    "AV 1017 is printed with the variable name CURRENT-YEAR but described as Current Minute; it is shown as printed.",
    "Heating setpoint is the cooling setpoint minus the heat offset (AV 10); AV 11 shows the result.",
    "Engineering units are not printed in the table. Source table: manual pages 30-31 (80 objects)."
  ],
